    "Disposition after initial evaluation involves deciding whether further workup can occur in an outpatient setting or if hospital-based evaluation is required. The main purpose of hospital evaluation is to expedite treatment of conditions identified or continue diagnostic evaluation for suspected syncope causes. This decision is complicated by varying resources and lack of consensus on risk thresholds. Hospital evaluation and treatment are advised for patients with syncope and a serious medical condition related to the syncope cause. Patients with presumptive reflex-mediated syncope can often be managed outpatient, unless exceptions apply, such as repeated syncope with risk of injury.": [],
